# Battle System Architecture

## Core Principles
- Focus on iterative development
- Maintain clear separation of battle phases
- Preserve real-time combat mechanics
- Ensure smooth animations and transitions

## Battle Flow

### 1. Pre-Battle Phase (3 seconds)
- Display countdown overlay
- Show deployment zones
- Animate network nodes and connection lines
- Initialize battalion health and positions

### 2. Active Battle Phase (20 seconds)
- Display battle timer at screen top
- Show battalion stats (health/quantity)
- Maintain animated network visualization

### 3. Combat Mechanics

#### Battalion Behavior
- Movement
  - Speed scaled by battalion speed stat
  - Follow network connection lines
  - Stop at attack range from target
  - Smooth animation transitions

- Combat
  - Attack power based on type and quantity
  - Health scaled by type and quantity
  - Damage triggers visual feedback
  - Destroyed battalions removed from field

#### Targeting System
- Initial Target Selection
  - Battalions target nearest node/enemy
  - Movement follows network paths
  - Attack range based on battalion type

- Retargeting Logic
  - Triggers when current target destroyed/captured
  - Prioritizes nearest valid target
  - Considers both nodes and enemy battalions
  - Immediately begins movement to new target

#### Node Control
- Node Health: 75% of total battalion health combined
- Control States
  - Enemy (Red)
  - Neutral (Purple)
  - User (Blue)
- Progress visualization during capture
- Affects battalion pathfinding

### 4. Victory Conditions
- All enemy battalions destroyed
- Most nodes controlled at timer end
- Least battalion losses at timer end

## Technical Requirements
- Efficient pathfinding along network
- Smooth animation transitions
- Real-time combat calculations
- Responsive retargeting system
- Accurate health/damage tracking
- Synchronized visual feedback